   "source": [
    "# Python Print Function\n",
    "\n",
    "## Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "- `print` is a Python built-in function name. A function performs some tasks.\n",
    "- Here it prints the message (a string, a number, etc.)  `\"Hello World!\"` to the console.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "![Alt Text](images\\print_function_diagram.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "![Alt Text](images\\print_function.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**What you'll learn:**\n",
    "- Basic print syntax\n",
    "- Printing multiple values\n",
    "- Using separators and end parameters\n",
    "- Escape sequences\n",
    "- String formatting with print\n",
    "- Printing different data types"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Part 1: Comprehensive Practice\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.1 Basic Print Statement"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Hello, World!\n",
      "42\n",
      "3.14159\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Simple print statement\n",
    "print(\"Hello, World!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print numbers\n",
    "print(42)\n",
    "print(3.14159)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.2 Printing Multiple Values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Print multiple items separated by comma\n",
    "print(\"Python\", \"is\", \"awesome\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print mix of strings and numbers\n",
    "print(\"I am\", 25, \"years old\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print multiple data types\n",
    "print(\"Integer:\", 100, \"Float:\", 3.14, \"String:\", \"Hello\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.3 The 'sep' Parameter (Separator)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Default separator is a space\n",
    "print(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Cherry\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Custom separator with dash\n",
    "print(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Cherry\", sep=\"-\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Custom separator with comma\n",
    "print(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Cherry\", sep=\", \")\n",
    "\n",
    "# No separator\n",
    "print(\"Apple\", \"Banana\", \"Cherry\", sep=\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Separator with newline\n",
    "print(\"First\", \"Second\", \"Third\", sep=\"\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Separator with multiple characters\n",
    "print(\"Python\", \"Java\", \"C++\", sep=\" | \")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.4 The 'end' Parameter"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Default end is newline (\\n)\n",
    "print(\"Hello\")\n",
    "print(\"World\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"---\")  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Custom end parameter - no newline\n",
    "print(\"Hello\", end=\" \")\n",
    "print(\"World\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"---\")  \n",
    "\n",
    "# End with different characters\n",
    "print(\"Python\", end=\"***\")\n",
    "print(\"Programming\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"---\")  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Combining multiple prints on same line\n",
    "print(\"Loading\", end=\"\")\n",
    "print(\".\", end=\"\")\n",
    "print(\".\", end=\"\")\n",
    "print(\".\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.5 Combining 'sep' and 'end' Parameters"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Using both sep and end together\n",
    "print(\"Apple\", \"BanananA\", \"Cherry\", sep=\" | \", end=\" <-- Fruits\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Creating formatted output\n",
    "print(\"Name\", \"Age\", \"City\", sep=\" - \", end=\" (Header)\\n\")\n",
    "print(\"John\", \"25\", \"New York\", sep=\" - \", end=\" (Data)\\n\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.6 Escape Sequences"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Newline (\\n)\n",
    "print(\"First Line\\nSecond Line\\nThird Line\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"---\")  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Tab (\\t)\n",
    "print(\"Name:\\tJohn\")\n",
    "print(\"Age:\\t25\")\n",
    "print(\"City:\\tNew York\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"---\")  \n",
    "\n",
    "# Backslash (\\\\)\n",
    "print(\"This is a backslash: \\\\\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Single quote (\\')\n",
    "print('It\\'s a beautiful day')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Double quote (\\\")\n",
    "print(\"She said, \\\"Hello!\\\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"---\")  # Separator\n",
    "\n",
    "# Carriage return (\\r) - moves cursor to beginning\n",
    "print(\"Hello\\rWorld\")  # World overwrites Hello\n",
    "\n",
    "# Backspace (\\b)\n",
    "print(\"Helloo\\b\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.7 Raw Strings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Regular string with escape sequences\n",
    "print(\"C:\\new\\test\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Raw string (r prefix) - ignores escape sequences\n",
    "print(r\"C:\\new\\test\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Useful for file paths \n",
    "print(r\"C:\\Users\\Student\\Documents\\file.txt\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.8 Printing Different Data Types"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Integer\n",
    "print(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Float\n",
    "print(3.14159)\n",
    "\n",
    "# String\n",
    "print(\"Hello, Python!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Boolean\n",
    "print(True)\n",
    "print(False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# List\n",
    "print([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tuple\n",
    "print((10, 20, 30))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Dictionary\n",
    "print({\"name\": \"John\", \"age\": 25})\n",
    "\n",
    "# None\n",
    "print(None)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.9 String Concatenation in Print"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Using + operator (only works with strings)\n",
    "print(\"Hello\" + \" \" + \"World\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# This will cause error - cannot concatenate string and number\n",
    "# print(\"I am \" + 25 + \" years old\")  # Uncomment to see error\n",
    "\n",
    "# Solution: Convert number to string\n",
    "print(\"I am ilyas \" + str(25) + \" years old\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Better approach: use comma (automatic conversion)\n",
    "print(\"I am\", 25, \"years old\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.10 String Formatting Methods"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Method 1: Using % operator (old style)\n",
    "name = \"Alice\"\n",
    "age = 30\n",
    "print(\"My name is %s and I am %d years old\" % (name, age))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Method 2: Using .format() method\n",
    "print(\"My name is {} and I am {} years old\".format(name, age))\n",
    "print(\"My name is {0} and I am {1} years old. Yes, {0}!\".format(name, age))\n",
    "print(\"My name is {n} and I am {a} years old\".format(n=name, a=age))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Method 3: Using f-strings (modern and recommended)\n",
    "print(f\"My name is {name} and I am {age} years old\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# F-strings with expressions\n",
    "print(f\"Next year I will be {age + 1} years old\")\n",
    "print(f\"My name in uppercase: {name.upper()}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.11 Formatting Numbers in Print"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Floating point precision\n",
    "pi = 3.14159265359\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Pi with 2 decimals: {pi:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Pi with 4 decimals: {pi:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Large numbers with comma separator\n",
    "big_number = 1234567890\n",
    "print(f\"Formatted number: {big_number:,}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Percentage formatting\n",
    "score = 0.856\n",
    "print(f\"Score: {score:.1%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scientific notation\n",
    "print(f\"Scientific: {big_number:.2e}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.12 Print with Width and Alignment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Right alignment (default for numbers)\n",
    "print(f\"{'Python':>15}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{42:>15}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Left alignment\n",
    "print(f\"{'Python':<15}***\")\n",
    "print(f\"{42:<15}***\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Center alignment\n",
    "print(f\"{'Python':^15}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{42:^15}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# With fill characters\n",
    "print(f\"{'Python':*^20}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Hello':-<20}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{100:0>10}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.13 Printing Empty Lines and Special Cases"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Print empty line\n",
    "print()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print multiple empty lines\n",
    "print(\"\\n\\n\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print nothing (empty string)\n",
    "print(\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print just spaces\n",
    "print(\"     \")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.14 Practical Examples"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Creating a simple receipt\n",
    "print(\"=\"*40)\n",
    "print(\"RECEIPT\".center(40))\n",
    "print(\"=\"*40)\n",
    "print(f\"{'Item':<20} {'Price':>10}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*40)\n",
    "print(f\"{'Apple':<20} ${3.99:>9.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Banana':<20} ${2.50:>9.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Orange':<20} ${4.25:>9.2f}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\"*40)\n",
    "print(f\"{'Total':<20} ${10.74:>9.2f}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*40)\n",
    "\n",
    "print()  # Empty line\n",
    "\n",
    "# Creating a simple table\n",
    "print(f\"{'Name':<15} {'Age':>5} {'City':<15}\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 37)\n",
    "print(f\"{'Alice':<15} {25:>5} {'New York':<15}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Bob':<15} {30:>5} {'Los Angeles':<15}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'Charlie':<15} {28:>5} {'Chicago':<15}\")"
   ]
  },
